 "prof.h":"👤 My profile","prof.name":"Name (shown in the header)","hello":"Hi, {name}!","prof.industry":"Industry","prof.tenure":"Tenure, years","prof.kids0":"Children under 6","prof.kids6":"Children 6–17","prof.extra":"Extra credit points","prof.hish":"I have keren hishtalmut (7.5% / 2.5%)",
 "brk.hish":"Keren hishtalmut (2.5%)","employer.hish":"Employer keren hishtalmut (7.5%)","ot.add":"➕ Add to gross in the calculator",
 "ai.t.morepoints":"<b>More credit points you may be owed (set in Form 101; missed in the past — tax refund up to 6 years back):</b><br>• Academic degree: BA — 1 point for a year after graduation, MA — 0.5.<br>• Alimony to an ex-spouse — +1 point for the payer.<br>• Single parent — extra points.<br>• 100% disability / blindness — not points but an income-tax exemption (sec. 9(5)).<br>• Residents of peripheral towns — a 7–20% income discount (by list; check your town in the Tax Authority simulator).<br>Enter your points in “Extra credit points” in the profile — the net recalculates.",
 "prof.ind.general":"General","prof.ind.cleaning":"Cleaning","prof.ind.security":"Security","prof.ind.construction":"Construction","prof.ind.catering":"Catering","prof.ind.care":"Caregiving",
 "prof.hint":"Your profile is stored on the device and tunes the whole app. Child credit points are counted automatically: under 6 — 4.5 points to each parent, 6–17 — mother 2 / father 1. Important: points apply only to children living with you in Israel — no points for children who stayed abroad (birth year and the year of turning 18 give partial points). Don't forget to mark the children in Form 101!",
 "prof.hish.hint":"<b>What it is:</b> keren hishtalmut — your personal tax-advantaged savings pot, a “second pension”.<br><b>How it fills up each month:</b><br>• 2.5% — from your pay;<br>• 7.5% — the employer adds on top, from their pocket;<br>• total: 10% lands in your account.<br><b>When you can take it:</b> after 6 years — the whole amount, tax-free.<br><b>Who gets it:</b> in cleaning, security and construction it is mandatory by law (extension order). Elsewhere — if your contract says so. See a השתלמות line in the payslip → tick the box.<br><b>Nuance:</b> the percentages apply to the base salary with fixed supplements — overtime and one-off bonuses are excluded (the app calculates it that way).",
 "fired.h":"Dismissal calculator: what am I owed","fired.hint":"A legal-minimum estimate for dismissal by the employer (or equivalent resignation). Fill in — see the full settlement.",
 "fired.paytype":"Pay type","fired.monthly":"Monthly","fired.hourlyp":"Hourly",
 "fired.gross":"Last gross, ₪/month","fired.tenure":"Tenure, years","fired.vacdays":"Unused vacation days","fired.havdays":"Unpaid havra'a days",
 "fired.res.pitz":"Severance (salary × years)","fired.res.notice":"Notice pay (if not allowed to work it)","fired.res.vac":"Vacation payout","fired.res.hav":"Havra'a","fired.total":"Total settlement",
 "fired.note":"Sec. 14: if the employer paid the full 8.33% severance into the fund — you collect that part from the pension fund, not from them directly. Vacation day rate = gross ÷ 21.67 (5-day week); havra'a uses your sector's daily rate (cleaning/security — ₪511.60). This is the legal minimum — extension orders may give more. The employment-period certificate is due within 14 days; register at the employment bureau on your first free day. ⚠️ Vacation claims — up to 3 years; wages and severance — up to 7.",
 "emp.ot.exp":"➕ This month's overtime (125% / 150%)","emp.ot.hint":"The hourly rate is taken automatically: gross ÷ 182. The overtime pay joins the taxable gross — income tax and National Insurance are computed on the full amount, while pension and hishtalmut, as the law requires, are computed on the base salary only.",
